  axialTiltDeg: 3.13
  atmosphericComposition: 'Primarily hydrogen and helium, with smaller quantities

    of
    methane, ammonia, water vapour and other compounds.

    Its visible cloud layers
    contain ammonia and other

    chemical compounds.'
  atmosphericPressureBar: 0
  minimumTemperatureC: 0
  meanTemperatureC: -110
  maximumTemperatureC: 0
  moonCount: 115
  notableMoons:
  - Io
  - Europa
  - Ganymede
  - Callisto
  internalStructure: 'Jupiter has a deep hydrogen-rich interior, including

    metallic
    hydrogen under extreme pressure and a

    central region containing heavier
    elements.'
  surfaceAndRings: 'Jupiter has no solid surface accessible like Earth''s.

    It
    possesses a faint ring system made mainly of dust.

    Its atmosphere contains
    cloud bands, vortices and

    the Great Red Spot.'
  magneticField: 'Jupiter has the strongest planetary magnetic field

    in the
    Solar System, generated by electrical currents

    in its metallic hydrogen
    interior.'
